{
  "note": [
    "A CENSUS OF THE LIVE CHAIN \u2014 the independent oracle for the JobBoard cut.",
    "",
    "This is not a list written here and not a restatement of the script. It is Base Sepolia's",
    "own answer to 'which selectors are mounted in the diamond today', read through",
    "the loupe. The composition of the cut (script/UpgradeJobBoardApplicantGate.s.sol)",
    "is held against THIS, not against itself.",
    "",
    "WHY IT MATTERS MORE HERE THAN IT DID FOR THE LAST CUT. That one only ADDED, so",
    "the only question was 'is any of them mounted already'. This one REPLACES a whole",
    "facet, and a Replace/Add pair is the operation that drops a cut on one live",
    "transaction: Replace reverts 'Diamond: selector not found' on a selector that is",
    "not mounted, Add reverts 'Diamond: selector exists' on one that is. So two claims",
    "have to be proved, and neither may be taken from the script:",
    "",
    "  * every selector the rebuilt facet exposes is mounted TODAY -> all of them",
    "    belong in Replace and the Add group is empty;",
    "  * every selector mounted on the JobBoard facet today is still exposed by the",
    "    rebuilt facet -> nothing is left behind pointing at a facet that no longer",
    "    implements it.",
    "",
    "The other side of both comparisons is solc's own methodIdentifiers for",
    "JobBoardFacet, read out of the build artifact. Neither side is computed from the",
    "other.",
    "",
    "STATE OF THE BOARD AT THE SAME READING: totalJobs = 5, and getApplicants() over",
    "ids 5..8, 10, 42 and 1000000 all answered [] \u2014 nobody had taken a future id yet.",
    "That is the measurement the second half of the fix is insurance against, not",
    "proof that it is unnecessary: the hole is described in a public repository, and",
    "the window stays open until this cut lands."
  ],
